# p_b8c2 — Omar litters out at lunch; Marco stays; separate evenings

Omar leaves the house for lunch 12:00–13:30 on weekdays (keys, wallet, jacket, sunglasses go with him). Marco remains at his desk in the bedroom. They eat dinner at different times: Omar 18:00, Marco 19:00. There is no shared TV. Omar reads in the armchair 20:00–22:00; Marco meditates 20:00–20:30 in the bedroom then reads at the nightstand 20:30–22:00. Weekends: sleep in until 10:00, errands 11:00–13:00 (both out), lunch 13:30, separate evenings. What sets this apart: jacket_omar and keys_omar are OUT_OF_HOUSE 12:00–13:30 weekdays while jacket_marco and keys_marco remain at the entry. The remote is never on the TV stand during 20:00–22:00 (no shared TV). Refuted if: both residents are sighted in the living room together at 20:30 on a weekday, or if keys_omar are at entry_table_e1 at 12:30 on a weekday.

