# p_e1a5 — Marco runs in the evening after dinner; Omar watches TV alone

Marco runs 19:30–20:15 on weekdays, after dinner. His running shoes and water bottle go OUT_OF_HOUSE. Omar stays home and watches TV 19:30–22:00 (alone, since Marco is out). They resume shared time at 20:15. Weekends: no running; Marco tends the balcony garden 10:00–10:45 (watering can, gardening gloves in use). Dinner 18:30–19:15. Work 9:00–17:30 both. What sets this apart: running_shoes_marco are OUT_OF_HOUSE 19:30–20:15 weekdays (not in the morning). The watering can is at balcony_table_y1 (in use) 10:00–10:45 weekends. Refuted if: running shoes are at shoe_rack_e1 at 19:45 on a weekday, or if the watering can is at balcony_floor_y1 at 10:15 on a Saturday.

