# p_a1b2 — Standard dual-WFH; nothing leaves the house

Two remote workers share this home. Both sit at their desks from 9 to 17:30 on weekdays and never leave during work hours. Keys, wallets, and jackets stay at the entry all day. Meals happen at the kitchen table for breakfast and lunch, at the dining table for dinner. In the evening both settle onto the couch for TV from 20:00 to 22:30, pulling the blanket and remote to the coffee table. On weekends they sleep in until about 10:30, do errands together around midday, and are home the rest of the day. Nothing in this household travels: no one goes to a gym, no one commutes, and the only time objects leave is a brief weekend errand where both walk out with keys and wallets. What sets this hypothesis apart: every personal object (keys, wallets, jackets, shoes) is inside the house at all times except a short weekend window. What would refute it: any personal object sighted OUT_OF_HOUSE on a weekday, or keys missing from the entry table during 9-to-5 work hours.

